  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Create the NEW append-only `sprk_emailreviewlog` audit entity so every AI proposal AND every human decision is queryable per matter (FR-08). This is the compliance differentiator (G-5): machine-review and human-review are BOTH written as rows. Job B apply (031) writes an audit row on every confirmed proposal; the triage/proposal path writes a row for every AI suggestion.

    **VERIFY-OR-CREATE**: the operator may have pre-created this entity in a parallel schema pass. FIRST check via Dataverse MCP `describe` whether `sprk_emailreviewlog` exists; if it exists, RECONCILE its attribute set against this spec (flag any missing/mismatched column; do NOT retype an in-use field). CREATE the entity + any missing attributes only if absent.

    Create the entity with (use Spaarke naming conventions; verify option-set integer conventions via MCP before any Choice):

    1. **`sprk_communication` lookup** (the reviewed item — the email; per FR-08 "item"). Enables per-matter query via the email's regarding.
    2. **`sprk_actortype`** — Choice: `machine` (rule/model) vs `human` (user). Both are first-class rows.
    3. **`sprk_actor`** — the actor identity: a `systemuser` lookup when human, OR a text rule/model id when machine (a text field carrying the model/rule id is acceptable; model the two-target case per Spaarke conventions — do NOT invent a polymorphic mechanism).
    4. **`sprk_action`** — Choice: the decision/action taken (e.g. AI-proposed / human-approved / human-rejected / human-edited — confirm the closed set at task time).
    5. **`sprk_aisuggestion`** — the prior AI suggestion as JSON (multiline Text): what the model proposed (old→new / category / etc.) so the human decision is auditable against it.
    6. **`sprk_confidence`** — Decimal (0–1), the AI suggestion's confidence at proposal time.
    7. **`sprk_sourceref`** — the cited source locator (email/attachment + locator) tying the suggestion to exact source text (NFR-06 trust/audit).
    8. **`sprk_targetentity` / `sprk_targetfield`** (optional, for Job B rows) — the record + field the proposal targeted (old→new lives in the JSON).
    9. **Timestamp** — creation timestamp (use the platform `createdon` if sufficient; add an explicit `sprk_occurredat` only if the audit semantics need it).

    Enforce **append-only** semantics via Spaarke conventions (no update/delete surface for normal actors; security-role / form config as the convention allows). Deploy to the project solution. This is schema ONLY — the write LOGIC (Job B apply audit row) is task 031.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke Dataverse schema engineer. Fluent in the `dataverse-create-schema` skill (Web API + PowerShell), append-only audit-entity modeling, and typed-vs-text actor identity. You create exactly the entity FR-08 needs — machine and human review both as rows — with a defensible per-email audit trail, and you verify-before-create so an operator's parallel pass is reconciled, not duplicated.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A NEW `sprk_emailreviewlog` entity exists (verify-or-create-reconciled) with: a `sprk_communication` lookup (item), `sprk_actortype` (machine/human), `sprk_actor` (systemuser lookup or model/rule id), `sprk_action`, `sprk_aisuggestion` JSON, `sprk_confidence` decimal, `sprk_sourceref` locator, optional `sprk_targetentity`/`sprk_targetfield`, and a timestamp — with append-only semantics. Both an AI proposal and a human decision can be written as distinct rows and queried per matter. Task 031 (Job B apply) can write the audit row against real schema. No existing entity/column retyped.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      NFR-06 (trust &amp; audit): every AI proposal carries a plain-language reason + citation to exact source text, and nothing record-mutating auto-finalizes. FR-08 makes this queryable: an append-only log where machine-review (the AI proposal) and human-review (the confirm/reject/edit decision) are BOTH rows, so per matter you can prove "AI proposed X from email Y at confidence Z; human approved/rejected at time T." Today there is no such entity — `AuditEnrichmentMiddleware` logs requests, not per-email review decisions (spec §New-Components). This task creates the entity; task 031 writes rows into it on Job B apply.

      §11 Component Justification (new entity): (1) **Existing overlap** — `AuditEnrichmentMiddleware` (request logs) cannot prove per-email human+machine review (task 001 / grep-confirmed). (2) **Extension instead** — request logs are the wrong grain; there is no existing per-email review entity to extend. (3) **Concrete cost-of-doing-nothing** — without it there is no defensible per-email review record; the compliance differentiator (G-5, success-criterion 9 "every AI proposal + human decision queryable per matter") fails and Job B apply (031) has nowhere to write its audit row (FR-10 acceptance fails). Named contract failures, not "future flexibility."
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/001-operator-schema-verification.md (task 001 output — whether `sprk_emailreviewlog` already exists; consume)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/spec.md (FR-08, FR-10, NFR-06, §New-Components — the compliance differentiator)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/UpdateRecordActionCore.cs (the Job B write core task 031 wraps; the audit row records its old→new + citation)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-08">Create `sprk_emailreviewlog` with: item (`sprk_communication` lookup), actor-type (machine/human), actor (user or model/rule id), action, prior AI suggestion + confidence, source-ref, timestamp — machine-review AND human-review BOTH as rows. Verify-before-create; reconcile any operator-pre-created shape.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-06">The `sprk_sourceref` locator + `sprk_aisuggestion` JSON MUST let an auditor tie a suggestion to exact cited source text; the schema supports "verify the cited text exists" (the verification logic is 030/031).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (append-only)">Enforce append-only semantics per Spaarke conventions — no normal-actor update/delete surface. MUST NOT model this as a mutable record.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Model the actor two-target case (systemuser vs model/rule id) with typed conventions; MUST NOT invent a new polymorphic identity mechanism. Verify Choice integer conventions via MCP before creating `sprk_actortype`/`sprk_action`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-027">Author the entity into the project's managed solution per subscription-isolation/solution conventions; no direct prod-only unmanaged changes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Schema ONLY. No write logic (Job B apply audit row is task 031), no BFF code.</constraint>
  </constraints>

