  <justification>
    <existing>`AuditEnrichmentMiddleware` logs BFF requests, not per-email review decisions; task 001 confirms no per-email review entity exists.</existing>
    <extension>Request logs are the wrong grain and cannot prove machine+human review of a specific email; there is no existing per-email review entity to extend, so a new append-only entity is the minimal surface.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it there is no defensible per-email review record: success-criterion 9 (every AI proposal + human decision queryable per matter) fails and Job B apply (031) has nowhere to write its audit row (FR-10 fails). Concrete contract failures.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read task 001's note (whether `sprk_emailreviewlog` exists) + spec FR-08/FR-10/NFR-06 + `UpdateRecordActionCore.cs` (what Job B apply will record) to fix the exact attribute set + confirm the `sprk_actortype`/`sprk_action` closed value sets.</step>
    <step order="2">Via Dataverse MCP `describe`, check whether `sprk_emailreviewlog` exists; if present, enumerate its attributes and reconcile against this spec (flag missing/mismatched columns; do NOT retype an in-use field).</step>
    <step order="3">Create the entity (if absent) + any missing attributes via `dataverse-create-schema`: `sprk_communication` lookup, `sprk_actortype` (Choice), `sprk_actor` (systemuser lookup + model/rule-id text), `sprk_action` (Choice), `sprk_aisuggestion` (multiline JSON), `sprk_confidence` (Decimal 0–1), `sprk_sourceref`, optional `sprk_targetentity`/`sprk_targetfield`, timestamp. Verify Choice integer conventions via MCP first.</step>
    <step order="4">Configure append-only semantics per Spaarke conventions (security-role / form config so normal actors cannot update/delete rows). Deploy to the project solution.</step>
    <step order="5">Verify: a row can be created for a machine actor AND a human actor against the same `sprk_communication` item; both are queryable per matter (via the item's regarding); rows are not updatable/deletable by a normal actor.</step>
    <step order="6">Document the created-entity inventory (logical names, types, targets, `sprk_actortype`/`sprk_action` value sets, `sprk_aisuggestion` JSON shape, append-only config) in `notes/012-emailreviewlog.md` for 031 + the §11 justification. Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (012 ✅) + `current-task.md`; confirm 031 unblocked.</step>
  </steps>

