    <criterion testable="true">The actor two-target case (systemuser vs model/rule id) is modeled with typed conventions — NO new polymorphic identity mechanism was invented.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: no existing entity/column was retyped; an operator-pre-created entity was reconciled, not duplicated; a type conflict was escalated.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 001 (whether the entity pre-exists → verify-or-create). Blocks 031 (Job B apply writes the audit row) and gates the deploy (060). The single most important property is the compliance grain: machine-review AND human-review must BOTH be rows tied to the same item — a design that only logs human decisions (or only AI proposals) fails FR-08/G-5. The write LOGIC is 031, not this task.
